  "problem": "The current CI subject changed after PR-002 and the existing WP0 v1.4.0 validation rejected it, while the original approval remains valid only for its exact historical evidence. The runner also needed an explicit, reviewable route for current WP0 validation without weakening the rest of the contract chain.",
  "resulting_behavior": "The candidate verifies the original WP0 v1.4.0 approval, evidence and receipt bytes in memory and checks their shared historical subject. It creates a current technical draft with a fresh subject, pending_authorized_review status, no current approval and no release or production eligibility. Only the exact reviewed WP0 v1.4.0 validate descriptor uses that verifier; WP0 tests and all other packages retain normal execution. Future versions use their strict normal path, child nonzero results remain failures, and a real zero-test child is rejected. Candidate commits before C3 are 0d82cb98dc7ea1791f84bb471d5c8d2800d96715, 86b7f7e6c875e877653dc6ff13e3850f7afa2743 and 7cfbb96096d5eba46c37fb5b1885f116aa82ab80; C3 files are prepared for the controller to commit and bind externally.",
